

3
00:04:23,541 --> 00:04:24,875
Madam...

4
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,250
I really have a bad
feeling about this place.

5
00:04:27,375 --> 00:04:30,125
So, let's get out of here
as soon as possible.

6
00:04:57,041 --> 00:04:59,041
Bring her alone.

7
00:04:59,291 --> 00:05:02,333
I don't want them
together even after death.

8
00:05:47,541 --> 00:05:49,125
Bring him!

9
00:06:00,208 --> 00:06:01,666
Go, find him.

10
00:06:13,208 --> 00:06:15,125
James...

11
00:06:16,875 --> 00:06:19,916
James, where are you?

12
00:06:20,750 --> 00:06:22,708
Don't play with me.

13
00:06:22,833 --> 00:06:24,250
Come to me.

14
00:06:27,083 --> 00:06:28,750
James...

15
00:06:28,875 --> 00:06:31,125
Where are you hiding?

16
00:06:31,250 --> 00:06:33,375
Come near me.

17
00:06:53,750 --> 00:06:55,541
James...

18
00:06:55,666 --> 00:06:58,125
Why are you so scared?

19
00:06:58,833 --> 00:07:00,416
Come to me.

20
00:07:00,666 --> 00:07:02,458
Come and kiss me!

21
00:07:03,583 --> 00:07:05,791
Just like our first time!

22
00:07:05,916 --> 00:07:08,375
Come on! Get up!

23
00:07:38,375 --> 00:07:44,583
'SAMBHAVAM ADHYAYAM ONNU'
[THE INCIDENT-CHAPTER ONE]

24
00:10:50,166 --> 00:10:52,125
Why didn't you shoot?

25
00:11:45,458 --> 00:11:46,708
James...

26
00:11:47,333 --> 00:11:49,000
Where are you?

27
00:12:51,833 --> 00:12:54,083
Neetu's bystander?

28
00:12:54,916 --> 00:12:57,083
Is Neetu's bystander here?

29
00:12:57,375 --> 00:12:58,249
Yes.

30
00:12:58,250 --> 00:13:00,833
The doctor is calling you.
Please go inside.

31
00:13:01,375 --> 00:13:02,583
I'll update you.

32
00:13:05,625 --> 00:13:06,875
Have a seat.

33
00:13:08,625 --> 00:13:09,416
Everything okay?

34
00:13:09,541 --> 00:13:11,000
Hey, don't worry.

35
00:13:11,125 --> 00:13:12,125
She's doing better now.

36
00:13:12,250 --> 00:13:14,583
Her due date is on
the 24th, next month, right?

37
00:13:15,583 --> 00:13:17,291
We'll admit her on the 23rd.

38
00:13:17,416 --> 00:13:21,458
Come immediately if you notice
any pain or discomfort before then.

39
00:13:22,083 --> 00:13:24,083
Anand, why do you look so tense?

40
00:13:24,208 --> 00:13:26,208
You seem more
worried than Neetu.

41
00:13:26,333 --> 00:13:26,916
No...

42
00:13:27,041 --> 00:13:29,000
Are you stressed?
- No, no.

43
00:13:29,208 --> 00:13:31,666
Neetu is fine.
Don't worry at all.

44
00:13:33,541 --> 00:13:34,666
Alright then.

45
00:13:39,416 --> 00:13:41,958
You stay put. I'll handle it.

46
00:13:42,166 --> 00:13:44,791
As if folding two clothes
is some huge task!

47
00:13:45,166 --> 00:13:47,583
I've kept some money inside.

48
00:13:48,583 --> 00:13:50,541
I have no choice but to go.

49
00:13:51,208 --> 00:13:53,333
Anyway, we still
have one month, right?

50
00:13:53,458 --> 00:13:56,083
I'll go there,
check the situation...

51
00:13:56,208 --> 00:13:58,208
...and return on a leave
on medical grounds.

52
00:13:58,500 --> 00:14:00,541
Why are you overthinking this?

53
00:14:00,666 --> 00:14:02,791
I can handle things here.

54
00:14:02,916 --> 00:14:05,208
Moreover,
aunt is here to help me.

55
00:14:06,583 --> 00:14:08,250
Call him if anything comes up.

56
00:14:08,375 --> 00:14:10,166
Sir, you get going now.

57
00:14:12,458 --> 00:14:14,041
Eat on time, okay?

58
00:14:14,291 --> 00:14:15,958
Come on, get ready to go.

59
00:14:16,083 --> 00:14:17,208
Go... go.

60
00:14:17,458 --> 00:14:18,666
Are you sure you're okay?

61
00:14:18,791 --> 00:14:20,833
I'm fine. Go ahead.
Don't worry about me.

62
00:14:20,958 --> 00:14:21,958
Okay?

63
00:14:44,458 --> 00:14:46,125
Hey, get down here.

64
00:14:57,250 --> 00:14:58,500
So, he went to the Gulf, huh?

65
00:14:58,625 --> 00:14:59,833
Chetta, one tea, please.

66
00:14:59,958 --> 00:15:01,458
How do I get to Velloorkadu?

67
00:15:01,583 --> 00:15:03,250
Just get into that jeep.

68
00:15:11,041 --> 00:15:11,833
Yeah, go ahead.

69
00:15:11,958 --> 00:15:13,958
Hey, have you reached?
- Not yet.

70
00:15:14,083 --> 00:15:16,125
Listen, she had some mild pain.

71
00:15:16,250 --> 00:15:17,958
So we're at the hospital now.

72
00:15:18,291 --> 00:15:20,000
What did the doctor say?!

73
00:15:20,166 --> 00:15:21,500
There's a slight complication.

74
00:15:21,625 --> 00:15:24,541
They're saying the delivery
might have to be done today itself.

75
00:15:25,833 --> 00:15:27,958
I'll come there right away.
- No need.

76
00:15:28,083 --> 00:15:29,541
You go ahead and join.

77
00:15:29,666 --> 00:15:31,250
You can't get here
anytime soon anyway.

78
00:15:31,375 --> 00:15:33,500
I just called to let you know.
No need to worry.

79
00:15:33,625 --> 00:15:35,375
Aunt is there, right?
- Yes.

80
00:15:35,500 --> 00:15:36,875
Don't worry.
I'll keep you posted.

81
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,000
Okay.

82
00:15:43,875 --> 00:15:46,500
If you're coming,
just get into the vehicle.

83
00:15:49,041 --> 00:15:51,083
Chetta, cancel the tea.
- Huh?

84
00:15:56,708 --> 00:15:58,250
Where are you barging in!?

85
00:15:58,375 --> 00:15:59,541
Get in the backside!

86
00:16:02,333 --> 00:16:04,166
Who the heck is he?

87
00:16:33,583 --> 00:16:34,791
Are you hungry?

88
00:16:39,916 --> 00:16:41,541
What's wrong, sir?

89
00:16:41,916 --> 00:16:43,208
Nothing.

90
00:16:43,333 --> 00:16:45,083
Is your SIM BSNL?

91
00:16:45,333 --> 00:16:46,333
No.

92
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:49,250
Only BSNL gets signal here.

93
00:16:49,375 --> 00:16:51,541
If it's urgent,
you can call from this phone.

94
00:16:54,666 --> 00:16:56,916
Go on, make the call.
- No need.

95
00:16:57,041 --> 00:16:59,458
If you're planning to call
your wife or someone,

96
00:16:59,583 --> 00:17:01,666
it's better not to
call from his phone.

97
00:17:01,791 --> 00:17:03,250
Right, Shaji?

98
00:17:06,333 --> 00:17:08,500
Ignore them.
You go ahead, sir.

99
00:17:36,125 --> 00:17:37,541
Not answering?

100
00:17:37,666 --> 00:17:38,666
No.

101
00:17:41,666 --> 00:17:42,666
Sir...

102
00:17:44,750 --> 00:17:45,416
Hello?

103
00:17:45,625 --> 00:17:47,708
Why aren't you answering me?

104
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,000
Neetu?

105
00:17:56,416 --> 00:17:57,416
Okay.

106
00:17:59,458 --> 00:18:00,458
I've become a father.

107
00:18:00,791 --> 00:18:01,791
Wow!

108
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:02,791
That's wonderful news.

109
00:18:02,916 --> 00:18:03,916
Boy or girl?

110
00:18:04,125 --> 00:18:05,125
It's a girl.

111
00:18:07,208 --> 00:18:09,375
Uncle's been blessed
with a baby girl.

112
00:18:10,166 --> 00:18:12,166
Congrats, Uncle.
- Thank you.

113
00:18:12,291 --> 00:18:13,958
Which grade are you in, dear?
- 4th grade.

114
00:18:14,083 --> 00:18:15,083
Ah, nice!

115
00:18:25,625 --> 00:18:26,750
Shaji, listen...

116
00:18:27,208 --> 00:18:29,916
Did you hear about
Ittichan's daughter?

117
00:18:30,041 --> 00:18:33,958
Heard she's shacked up
with someone in Bangalore.

118
00:18:34,083 --> 00:18:35,833
I heard that.
- And also...

119
00:18:35,958 --> 00:18:39,958
Makes you wonder why we even
bother educating girls these days.

120
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:52,583
O dear!

121
00:18:54,250 --> 00:18:56,125
Hey, open.

122
00:19:01,666 --> 00:19:02,791
Sir!

123
00:19:04,708 --> 00:19:06,083
Sir!

124
00:19:06,375 --> 00:19:07,708
Where's the closest hospital?

125
00:19:07,833 --> 00:19:09,208
Not close.
We'll have to go a bit.

126
00:19:09,333 --> 00:19:10,375
Hey!

127
00:19:10,583 --> 00:19:11,708
What are you doing?

128
00:19:11,833 --> 00:19:12,915
Let the police come, you moron!

129
00:19:12,916 --> 00:19:15,000
I'm the darn police,
you moron! Hold him!

130
00:19:18,291 --> 00:19:19,875
Come on.

131
00:19:20,666 --> 00:19:22,041
Careful.

132
00:19:23,458 --> 00:19:24,500
Yes, bring him.

133
00:19:28,416 --> 00:19:30,875
Open the door. I'll hold him.

134
00:19:32,041 --> 00:19:33,958
Start the vehicle.
- Uncle...

135
00:19:36,541 --> 00:19:38,583
Dear, go sit in the front.

136
00:19:47,041 --> 00:19:48,583
Hey, move aside!

137
00:19:50,583 --> 00:19:52,250
Get a rickshaw or something!

138
00:19:52,375 --> 00:19:53,500
Come on, man, let's go!

139
00:21:04,583 --> 00:21:07,250
Sir!
- Please, sit.

140
00:21:07,375 --> 00:21:09,625
Anandu, right?
- Anand, sir.

141
00:21:09,875 --> 00:21:10,500
Yeah.

142
00:21:10,875 --> 00:21:12,166
That's what I said.

143
00:21:12,625 --> 00:21:13,790
Where are you from, in Kerala?

144
00:21:13,791 --> 00:21:14,541
Kochi.

145
00:21:14,666 --> 00:21:16,625
So, you're a Kochi folk?

146
00:21:17,750 --> 00:21:18,833
Sir...

147
00:21:19,541 --> 00:21:22,208
Sir, I got this from him.

148
00:21:24,125 --> 00:21:26,625
Who? The guy who
just met with the accident?

149
00:21:31,541 --> 00:21:33,291
Peter John...

150
00:21:35,791 --> 00:21:37,000
Well...

151
00:21:37,125 --> 00:21:38,875
We'll have to report this

152
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:40,041
at Perumalai station.

153
00:21:40,166 --> 00:21:41,250
Take a photo of this.

154
00:21:42,208 --> 00:21:43,375
Might come in handy later.

155
00:21:43,500 --> 00:21:45,416
Sir, he seems to be alright.

156
00:21:45,541 --> 00:21:47,166
But he has lost some blood.

157
00:21:47,291 --> 00:21:49,166
Did you inform his family?
- I will.

158
00:21:49,458 --> 00:21:51,333
Wait till they get here.

159
00:21:51,791 --> 00:21:54,416
And those jeep people...

160
00:21:54,541 --> 00:21:57,458
Let them go only after
completing all the formalities.

161
00:21:57,583 --> 00:21:58,665
There's a reason for that.

162
00:21:58,666 --> 00:21:59,666
Did you have tea?

163
00:21:59,958 --> 00:22:00,625
No.

164
00:22:00,750 --> 00:22:01,416
Come.

165
00:22:01,541 --> 00:22:03,625
We get top-notch tea
in the canteen here.

166
00:22:03,875 --> 00:22:04,916
Come, let's grab some tea.

167
00:22:05,333 --> 00:22:06,416
Come on.

168
00:22:11,166 --> 00:22:12,583
Yeah, tell me.

169
00:22:12,708 --> 00:22:13,790
Your family?

170
00:22:13,791 --> 00:22:14,958
Just my wife.

171
00:22:15,416 --> 00:22:17,041
No... now I have a baby girl too.

172
00:22:17,625 --> 00:22:18,625
How old is your daughter?

173
00:22:18,875 --> 00:22:21,500
She was born today,
just a few hours back.

174
00:22:23,333 --> 00:22:25,208
Then he owes us a treat, sir.

175
00:22:26,500 --> 00:22:27,541
Why not?

176
00:22:27,791 --> 00:22:29,791
So you haven't even
seen your daughter yet?

177
00:22:31,416 --> 00:22:32,583
Do one thing...

178
00:22:32,916 --> 00:22:33,583
Just go back.

179
00:22:33,791 --> 00:22:34,875
Join first, then head back.

180
00:22:35,166 --> 00:22:36,750
No, sir. It's fine.

181
00:22:39,375 --> 00:22:40,375
Wait...

182
00:22:40,958 --> 00:22:42,040
You can do this.

183
00:22:42,041 --> 00:22:43,083
Go back on Sunday.

184
00:22:43,500 --> 00:22:45,208
Take a couple of days
and then come back.

185
00:22:46,625 --> 00:22:49,791
It's not like you've got some
huge responsibility here!

186
00:22:50,250 --> 00:22:52,250
No better place to
get transferred anyway!

187
00:22:52,375 --> 00:22:53,375
Yeah... yeah.

188
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:58,958
A disciplinary action, huh?

189
00:22:59,250 --> 00:23:00,625
You're not a troublemaker, are you?

190
00:23:00,875 --> 00:23:01,875
No, sir...

191
00:23:02,375 --> 00:23:05,041
We faced complications
during my wife's pregnancy.

192
00:23:05,750 --> 00:23:10,208
Almost every day after duty, I
couldn't sleep because of the tension.

193
00:23:10,750 --> 00:23:13,583
Then one day, I was on
guard duty... and I dozed off.

194
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:16,583
I missed saluting the SHO
when he came in.

195
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:20,000
No wonder...

196
00:23:20,208 --> 00:23:24,291
No wonder you put on
a whole show when I walked in.

197
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:26,041
Listen...

198
00:23:26,375 --> 00:23:28,500
Respect should
reflect in your conduct.

199
00:23:29,041 --> 00:23:32,291
Not just in snapping a salute
the moment you see someone.

200
00:23:32,833 --> 00:23:34,833
We don't follow that culture here.

201
00:23:35,833 --> 00:23:37,375
What about your parents?

202
00:23:39,916 --> 00:23:41,250
I've never seen my father.

203
00:23:41,583 --> 00:23:43,291
He was also in the
police department.

204
00:23:44,583 --> 00:23:46,791
He passed away
just before I was born.

205
00:23:47,458 --> 00:23:50,625
That shock broke
my mother mentally.

206
00:23:50,916 --> 00:23:52,625
Didn't take long...
she left too.

207
00:23:54,083 --> 00:23:57,625
Since it was a love marriage,
my wife's family doesn't talk to us.

208
00:23:58,875 --> 00:24:00,000
Now that you have a child...

209
00:24:00,333 --> 00:24:01,916
things will slowly
fall into place.

210
00:24:03,625 --> 00:24:05,250
Wasn't very different
for me either.

211
00:24:05,375 --> 00:24:06,500
Really?
- Yeah!

212
00:24:06,625 --> 00:24:08,833
He was in love with a girl.

213
00:24:09,291 --> 00:24:15,291
Her father was hell-bent on not
getting her married to him.

214
00:24:15,708 --> 00:24:17,500
He was ready to kill him
if it came to that.

215
00:24:17,875 --> 00:24:19,458
We didn't think twice.

216
00:24:19,916 --> 00:24:22,791
Taking the girl out of her
house, getting them married...

217
00:24:22,916 --> 00:24:25,333
And sending them straight
to their first night...

218
00:24:25,458 --> 00:24:28,125
The Kerala Police took
the entire responsibility!

219
00:24:28,541 --> 00:24:30,250
But now...

220
00:24:30,625 --> 00:24:33,708
He and his father-in-law
are like two peas in a pod now.

221
00:24:35,250 --> 00:24:37,208
That's all it takes, Anandu.

222
00:24:38,583 --> 00:24:40,041
Everything will be alright.

223
00:24:43,750 --> 00:24:44,958
Yes, Rasheed?

224
00:24:45,250 --> 00:24:46,541
Sir, there's an issue.

225
00:24:46,916 --> 00:24:48,083
What issue?

226
00:24:48,500 --> 00:24:50,958
While passing
through the forest road...

227
00:24:51,916 --> 00:24:54,833
We noticed a vehicle parked
suspiciously and checked it.

228
00:24:55,458 --> 00:24:56,875
Some youngsters were inside.

229
00:24:57,500 --> 00:24:59,875
They were trying to shoot some
video. They're Tamilians, sir.

230
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:02,500
There are 1-2 girls
with them too. - Okay.

231
00:25:03,333 --> 00:25:05,041
Sir, he's stepped
in and blocked them!

232
00:25:06,791 --> 00:25:08,000
Who? Reji?

233
00:25:08,208 --> 00:25:09,208
Yes, sir.

234
00:25:14,416 --> 00:25:16,833
Looks like they have
influence at higher levels.

235
00:25:17,416 --> 00:25:19,000
I don't think I can handle this.

236
00:25:19,541 --> 00:25:21,000
Sir, can you come here quickly?

237
00:25:24,833 --> 00:25:26,750
What the heck
is wrong with him!?

238
00:25:30,250 --> 00:25:31,500
Please don't create trouble.

239
00:25:31,625 --> 00:25:32,750
The SI will be here soon.

240
00:25:33,250 --> 00:25:34,458
Why should I talk to him, sir?

241
00:25:34,791 --> 00:25:36,583
Even now, we are
standing in our area.

242
00:25:36,708 --> 00:25:38,416
Son, just listen to me.

243
00:25:38,791 --> 00:25:41,500
Beyond this point, only the
Forest Department has permission.

244
00:25:41,708 --> 00:25:43,208
This is a restricted zone.

245
00:25:43,416 --> 00:25:45,000
Sir, I understand that.

246
00:25:45,333 --> 00:25:47,166
But why is he yelling
at me like that?

247
00:25:48,041 --> 00:25:49,666
Who is he? Some forest ranger?

248
00:25:50,125 --> 00:25:51,541
Tell him to calm down first.

249
00:25:51,666 --> 00:25:53,291
Or you can't imagine
what happens next!

250
00:25:54,208 --> 00:25:57,041
Listen, this area falls
under our father's control.

251
00:25:57,458 --> 00:25:59,000
If you create trouble
for us here...

252
00:25:59,333 --> 00:26:01,249
You can forget about
wearing that uniform again!

253
00:26:01,250 --> 00:26:04,416
If you want to keep your job,
leave right now!

254
00:26:04,541 --> 00:26:06,791
What is it, dad? Didn't I
tell you I'll call you later?!

255
00:26:10,583 --> 00:26:12,083
Hey, let go of my hand!

256
00:26:12,208 --> 00:26:13,375
Switch it off!

257
00:26:14,750 --> 00:26:17,208
I said switch it off now!
- Let go of me!

258
00:26:18,208 --> 00:26:19,999
Didn't I warn you clearly
the first time, you wretches?

259
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:21,541
Get out of here right now!

260
00:26:25,916 --> 00:26:27,833
Reji, Reji, no!

261
00:26:28,166 --> 00:26:30,166
Reji, stop!

262
00:26:33,916 --> 00:26:35,291
Hey, no!

263
00:26:35,500 --> 00:26:36,500
Reji!

264
00:26:36,666 --> 00:26:37,750
Reji, stop!

265
00:26:38,083 --> 00:26:39,208
Listen to me!

266
00:27:25,083 --> 00:27:27,000
Where?
- A little deeper inside, sir.

267
00:27:39,833 --> 00:27:41,541
Did you identify the person?
- No, sir.

268
00:27:41,875 --> 00:27:43,541
Something has chewed off his face.

269
00:27:43,875 --> 00:27:45,708
And his clothes are
soaked in mud too, sir.

270
00:27:46,166 --> 00:27:47,750
Looks like he fell into a marsh.

271
00:28:04,791 --> 00:28:06,125
Did you inform forensics?

272
00:28:06,291 --> 00:28:07,458
They're on the way, sir.

273
00:28:07,791 --> 00:28:09,458
It'll take some
time to reach here.

274
00:28:29,625 --> 00:28:30,666
What's got into you?

275
00:28:30,791 --> 00:28:32,832
You seem more bothered
than the Forest Department!

276
00:28:32,833 --> 00:28:33,958
Just because I gave you some

277
00:28:34,083 --> 00:28:36,208
freedom, don't push
your luck with me!

278
00:28:38,166 --> 00:28:39,666
Did you collect their details?

279
00:28:39,791 --> 00:28:40,791
Yes, sir.

280
00:28:41,208 --> 00:28:43,666
Sir... doesn't that look
like a policeman's body?

281
00:28:44,375 --> 00:28:46,625
Shouldn't we probe that angle?

282
00:28:46,875 --> 00:28:48,833
Oh, as if we're idiots!

283
00:28:50,708 --> 00:28:52,750
That's a policeman from
Perumalai station, sir.

284
00:28:53,125 --> 00:28:54,750
But they're not
answering calls right now.

285
00:28:54,916 --> 00:28:55,916
Who's this?

286
00:28:56,958 --> 00:28:58,333
I'm the new CPO, sir.

287
00:28:58,708 --> 00:29:01,082
Hey, do you have the number
of anyone from Perumalai station?

288
00:29:01,083 --> 00:29:01,625
No, sir.

289
00:29:02,041 --> 00:29:04,208
Sir, I have an ASI's
number from there.

290
00:29:04,416 --> 00:29:05,416
Give it.

291
00:29:07,208 --> 00:29:08,708
- 2-0
- 2-0...

292
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:11,000
- 9-5-0-3
- 9-5-0-3.

293
00:29:12,208 --> 00:29:17,041
'The number you are trying to reach
is currently out of reach.'

294
00:29:17,500 --> 00:29:19,250
You try reaching them too.
- Okay, sir.

295
00:29:20,041 --> 00:29:21,957
Report to the station when
the forensic team arrives.

296
00:29:21,958 --> 00:29:23,333
I'll be at the station.

297
00:29:27,500 --> 00:29:28,500
I'll come along.

298
00:29:29,000 --> 00:29:31,125
If anything comes up, call me.

299
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:33,250
Move in.

300
00:30:15,791 --> 00:30:17,208
Hey, Peter!

301
00:30:20,666 --> 00:30:21,916
Muthuvel!

302
00:30:24,416 --> 00:30:25,583
Peter!

303
00:30:28,750 --> 00:30:29,958
Muthuvel!

304
00:30:32,583 --> 00:30:34,750
Can anyone hear me?

305
00:30:36,083 --> 00:30:39,208
Can anyone hear me?

306
00:30:45,750 --> 00:30:47,750
P3 calling, P3 calling!

307
00:30:48,041 --> 00:30:49,625
Can anyone hear me?

308
00:30:49,750 --> 00:30:51,125
I repeat, can anyone hear me?

309
00:30:51,375 --> 00:30:52,416
Sir!

310
00:30:52,666 --> 00:30:54,250
Hello!

311
00:30:54,375 --> 00:30:55,708
Isn't this that officer's handset?

312
00:30:55,833 --> 00:30:57,833
'Can anyone hear me?'
- Sir, what's that?

313
00:30:58,208 --> 00:31:00,583
'We came into this
forest as a team, sir.'

314
00:31:00,708 --> 00:31:02,500
'Now the rest are missing.'

315
00:31:02,625 --> 00:31:04,208
'I'm the only one left.'

316
00:31:04,500 --> 00:31:06,416
'Please save me somehow, sir.'

317
00:31:06,583 --> 00:31:07,583
Hello?

318
00:31:07,708 --> 00:31:08,833
Sir! Sir! Sir! Sir!

319
00:31:08,958 --> 00:31:11,500
My name is Stephen, sir. Can
you hear me? Can you hear me?

320
00:31:11,625 --> 00:31:13,250
Yes, I can. I can hear you.

321
00:31:13,583 --> 00:31:14,833
My leg is injured, sir.

322
00:31:14,958 --> 00:31:16,583
Feels like I'm
dying from the pain.

323
00:31:17,083 --> 00:31:18,291
Please do something, sir.

324
00:31:18,416 --> 00:31:19,791
Sir, this is Kerala Police.

325
00:31:20,125 --> 00:31:21,916
One officer from
your department has

326
00:31:22,041 --> 00:31:23,666
met with an accident
on the forest road.

327
00:31:23,791 --> 00:31:26,375
His handset is currently
with the Kerala Police.

328
00:31:26,500 --> 00:31:29,333
Inform your control room
or report to your station.

329
00:31:29,458 --> 00:31:31,583
Sir... sir...
please listen to me, sir.

330
00:31:32,375 --> 00:31:34,208
I'm trying for a long while.

331
00:31:34,541 --> 00:31:36,416
But no one's answering.

332
00:31:37,708 --> 00:31:39,791
I can't even move, sir.

333
00:31:39,916 --> 00:31:42,208
I've lost a lot of blood...

334
00:31:42,708 --> 00:31:44,625
I'm near the temple, sir.

335
00:31:45,166 --> 00:31:46,541
Please come help me, sir.

336
00:31:46,833 --> 00:31:49,125
Sir, this is risky.
It's outside our limits.

337
00:31:49,416 --> 00:31:53,250
On top of that, we wont understand
anything if we get deep inside it.

338
00:31:55,125 --> 00:31:56,208
Sir...

339
00:31:56,541 --> 00:31:57,958
Are you there, sir?

340
00:31:58,708 --> 00:32:00,666
Please speak something, sir.

341
00:32:05,208 --> 00:32:06,583
Pull over the jeep.

342
00:32:22,916 --> 00:32:24,125
Hey, do you have network?

343
00:32:24,375 --> 00:32:25,375
No, sir.

344
00:32:26,291 --> 00:32:28,416
What the heck is wrong with him?

345
00:32:29,916 --> 00:32:31,708
That's a policeman
screaming for life, sir.

346
00:32:32,416 --> 00:32:33,583
Sir...

347
00:32:34,125 --> 00:32:35,583
are you in line?

348
00:32:37,208 --> 00:32:37,708
Sir...

349
00:32:37,833 --> 00:32:39,708
I'm going to have a baby, sir.

350
00:32:42,083 --> 00:32:45,375
We've waited for so many years
after our marriage.

351
00:32:46,041 --> 00:32:49,291
If you help me...
I can at least see my child.

352
00:32:50,250 --> 00:32:52,208
I'm begging you
like you're God, sir.

353
00:32:52,875 --> 00:32:54,000
Sir, please... sir!

354
00:32:54,541 --> 00:32:58,083
Switch off that Darn thing.
Hey, start the vehicle.

355
00:32:58,708 --> 00:33:01,125
Sir, he says he's
lost a lot of blood.

356
00:33:01,541 --> 00:33:03,958
If we don't help him now,
he'll bleed out to death there, sir.

357
00:33:04,166 --> 00:33:05,541
So what?

358
00:33:05,666 --> 00:33:06,875
That's not our responsibility.

359
00:33:07,083 --> 00:33:08,583
Sir, I know it isn't.

360
00:33:08,708 --> 00:33:11,166
But if we act now, he might at
least live to see his child.

361
00:33:11,500 --> 00:33:12,750
It's a life, sir.

362
00:33:12,875 --> 00:33:14,333
What nonsense are you talking?

363
00:33:14,791 --> 00:33:16,457
Have you ever stepped
into this forest before?

364
00:33:16,458 --> 00:33:17,791
I'm a local around here.

365
00:33:19,083 --> 00:33:21,125
Sir, this place is dangerous!

366
00:33:21,416 --> 00:33:23,707
If you want to go in trusting
some random guy, go ahead.

367
00:33:23,708 --> 00:33:24,708
I'm not coming.

368
00:33:24,958 --> 00:33:26,250
Sir, are you scared?

369
00:33:26,750 --> 00:33:27,750
Scared?

370
00:33:28,083 --> 00:33:29,083
Me?

371
00:34:18,833 --> 00:34:19,583
Sir!

372
00:34:19,708 --> 00:34:20,708
Hey!

373
00:34:21,000 --> 00:34:23,291
Hey, move away!

374
00:34:23,416 --> 00:34:24,666
What are you doing?

375
00:34:24,875 --> 00:34:26,791
I'll shoot him down!

376
00:34:28,625 --> 00:34:29,458
Put the gun down.

377
00:34:29,583 --> 00:34:31,958
Come on, let me go!

378
00:34:32,083 --> 00:34:34,208
Hey, hand over that gun!

379
00:34:34,333 --> 00:34:36,750
Listen to me.
Put the gun down!

380
00:34:36,875 --> 00:34:38,875
I'll kill him! I swear I will!

381
00:34:39,833 --> 00:34:41,375
Hey, unlock this!

382
00:34:43,416 --> 00:34:44,708
Hey!

383
00:34:49,250 --> 00:34:50,416
Don't shoot!

384
00:34:50,958 --> 00:34:52,625
Tell him to unlock this!

385
00:35:01,333 --> 00:35:03,291
Hey, hurry up!

386
00:35:04,125 --> 00:35:05,125
Go, go!

387
00:35:05,625 --> 00:35:08,458
Hey, stop right there!
- Come on!

388
00:35:08,666 --> 00:35:10,416
Hey, are you okay!?

389
00:35:10,625 --> 00:35:12,375
Peter, where's
the first-aid box?

390
00:35:12,500 --> 00:35:14,166
I'll get it right away, sir.
- Das...

391
00:35:14,375 --> 00:35:15,458
Are you okay?

392
00:38:10,541 --> 00:38:11,541
Peter!

393
00:38:13,416 --> 00:38:15,125
If you see them, don't shoot.

394
00:38:15,625 --> 00:38:17,333
Inform me first.

395
00:38:17,791 --> 00:38:19,541
Sir, do we really
need to go further?

396
00:38:29,375 --> 00:38:29,875
Sir...

397
00:38:30,166 --> 00:38:32,583
I don't believe in ghosts
or evil spirits that much.

398
00:38:32,833 --> 00:38:36,208
But ever since we entered here,
something feels very wrong.

399
00:38:38,625 --> 00:38:39,625
Sir...

400
00:38:39,916 --> 00:38:41,083
Since my childhood...

401
00:38:41,500 --> 00:38:44,375
there's a story everyone in the
village keeps talking about, sir.

402
00:38:44,791 --> 00:38:47,875
Many years ago, there
was a temple here.

403
00:38:48,541 --> 00:38:50,708
To drive away bad times
and bring good fortune,

404
00:38:51,000 --> 00:38:52,750
people used to
pray to that deity.

405
00:38:52,875 --> 00:38:56,833
The day people began
offering human sacrifices,

406
00:38:57,250 --> 00:38:59,500
that was the day all
the troubles began.

407
00:39:00,333 --> 00:39:02,041
From that day onwards,
on this soil...

408
00:39:02,291 --> 00:39:03,750
No blood should be spilled...

409
00:39:04,166 --> 00:39:06,208
And no sound should
cross a certain limit.

410
00:39:37,500 --> 00:39:39,916
Muthuvel, you go that way.
I'll take this route.

411
00:39:40,083 --> 00:39:42,208
Oh no, sir, please listen
to me for heaven's sake!

412
00:39:42,916 --> 00:39:44,125
Hey, Muthuvel...

413
00:39:44,333 --> 00:39:46,332
In those times, there were
plenty of stories like this.

414
00:39:46,333 --> 00:39:47,915
But we have to catch
them no matter what.

415
00:39:47,916 --> 00:39:49,249
We don't have any other choice.

416
00:39:49,250 --> 00:39:51,375
Go! Please understand. Go!

417
00:40:17,375 --> 00:40:19,666
Sir, please save me!

418
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:21,208
Sir!

419
00:40:21,541 --> 00:40:23,000
Sir!

420
00:40:35,208 --> 00:40:36,833
Muthuvel!

421
00:40:38,708 --> 00:40:39,708
Sir!

422
00:40:39,875 --> 00:40:40,750
What happened, Muthuvel?

423
00:40:40,875 --> 00:40:41,875
It's them!

424
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:44,833
Hey!

425
00:40:44,958 --> 00:40:46,541
Calm down. Surrender yourself.

426
00:40:48,583 --> 00:40:49,708
Hey!

427
00:41:19,666 --> 00:41:21,375
James!

428
00:41:21,666 --> 00:41:23,291
Where are you?

429
00:41:34,250 --> 00:41:35,791
Come here.

430
00:42:10,208 --> 00:42:11,208
Muthuvel?

431
00:42:11,375 --> 00:42:12,750
Hey, Muthuvel!

432
00:42:13,833 --> 00:42:14,833
Muthuvel!

433
00:42:15,291 --> 00:42:16,374
Muthuvel!

434
00:42:16,375 --> 00:42:17,875
Hey, Muthuvel!

435
00:42:18,000 --> 00:42:19,082
Peter!

436
00:42:19,083 --> 00:42:20,750
Where did you go?

437
00:42:41,458 --> 00:42:43,000
Sir, should we
really go any further?

438
00:42:43,166 --> 00:42:45,375
What happened? Already tired?

439
00:42:46,041 --> 00:42:47,250
Come on.

440
00:42:55,500 --> 00:42:56,875
Hey, Reji...

441
00:42:57,458 --> 00:43:01,250
You still buy into those
tall tales people spin?

442
00:43:06,125 --> 00:43:08,500
Sir, what are the locals
saying about this place?

443
00:43:08,791 --> 00:43:10,625
They've got plenty of stories.

444
00:43:11,000 --> 00:43:13,333
Many people have gone
missing in this forest.

445
00:43:13,541 --> 00:43:18,125
The first missing case was reported
in our station back in 1960.

446
00:43:18,416 --> 00:43:21,708
A girl who worked
at a nearby estate.

447
00:43:21,958 --> 00:43:25,000
The estate owner
was a Portuguese lady.

448
00:43:25,458 --> 00:43:27,750
People said she had
some strange issues.

449
00:43:28,041 --> 00:43:31,208
She married a man
much younger than her.

450
00:43:31,791 --> 00:43:34,916
That man was having an affair
with the girl who worked there.

451
00:43:37,291 --> 00:43:39,416
The Portuguese lady
caught them red-handed.

452
00:43:39,666 --> 00:43:40,832
She dragged both
of them into the forest

453
00:43:40,833 --> 00:43:42,083
and dumped their bodies there.

454
00:43:42,791 --> 00:43:44,583
Later, she also died.

455
00:43:48,375 --> 00:43:51,833
People say all three of their
spirits still wander around here.

456
00:43:53,416 --> 00:43:56,875
After I took charge, we recovered
a body from this forest once.

457
00:43:57,125 --> 00:44:00,708
Almost around the same place
where we found the body today.

458
00:44:00,958 --> 00:44:03,416
That man too... hadn't
been dead for long.

459
00:44:03,541 --> 00:44:05,750
The body had just
started decomposing.

460
00:44:06,125 --> 00:44:07,207
But...

461
00:44:07,208 --> 00:44:09,416
That body had no head!

462
00:44:14,833 --> 00:44:16,791
Aren't you coming?

463
00:44:19,458 --> 00:44:21,333
Sir, then what happened next?

464
00:44:21,458 --> 00:44:23,125
What else could happen?

465
00:44:23,416 --> 00:44:26,041
We couldn't identify
the body without the head.

466
00:44:26,541 --> 00:44:30,333
Locals started spinning stories,
said it was that foreigner.

467
00:44:30,458 --> 00:44:31,250
Who?

468
00:44:31,375 --> 00:44:33,833
That man who supposedly
died almost 80 years ago!

469
00:44:34,041 --> 00:44:36,416
Freaking nonsense,
their wild fantasies!

470
00:44:37,000 --> 00:44:38,457
Then did you ever
find the head, sir?

471
00:44:38,458 --> 00:44:39,500
No chance.

472
00:44:39,625 --> 00:44:41,916
We searched everywhere,
but found nothing.

473
00:44:42,041 --> 00:44:44,125
Back then, we never came
this deep into the forest.

474
00:44:44,500 --> 00:44:46,332
Honestly, this is my first
time coming this far inside.

475
00:44:46,333 --> 00:44:48,416
But back then, we
did recover a skull.

476
00:44:49,083 --> 00:44:50,916
Though it looked quite old.

477
00:44:51,458 --> 00:44:52,499
Whose was it?

478
00:44:52,500 --> 00:44:53,500
No idea.

479
00:44:53,833 --> 00:44:55,625
It could have belonged
to that foreigner.

480
00:44:59,791 --> 00:45:01,958
Sir, shouldn't we inform
the forest authorities?

481
00:45:02,208 --> 00:45:04,000
What? Are you scared too?

482
00:45:04,125 --> 00:45:05,166
No...

483
00:45:05,375 --> 00:45:06,750
According to him...

484
00:45:07,000 --> 00:45:08,291
this falls under another state.

485
00:45:08,416 --> 00:45:10,207
By the time we
inform them and they

486
00:45:10,208 --> 00:45:12,041
relay it to the
forest department...

487
00:45:12,166 --> 00:45:13,791
he might already be dead.

488
00:45:14,083 --> 00:45:17,000
We're talking about saving a
life here.. - Can you hear me?

489
00:45:17,625 --> 00:45:18,166
Have you arrived?

490
00:45:18,291 --> 00:45:21,791
Where? Where are
you? We're on the way.

491
00:45:22,375 --> 00:45:24,458
Sir, there's a huge tree here.

492
00:45:24,750 --> 00:45:26,333
It's covered with creepers...

493
00:45:26,458 --> 00:45:27,958
I'm right under it.
- What?

494
00:45:28,083 --> 00:45:29,833
Sir... err...

495
00:45:29,958 --> 00:45:32,500
It's like a money plant, sir.
- What plant?

496
00:45:32,833 --> 00:45:34,458
Some kind of creeper!
You heard me!?

497
00:45:34,583 --> 00:45:36,958
Sir, do you understand?

498
00:45:50,083 --> 00:45:52,125
Sir, about that
hospital matter...

499
00:45:52,916 --> 00:45:54,375
Yeah, let me try calling Joshy.

500
00:45:56,416 --> 00:45:58,708
Hello, sir?
- Joshy, what's the update?

501
00:45:58,833 --> 00:46:00,082
Sir, he regained consciousness.

502
00:46:00,083 --> 00:46:01,583
He's blabbering
without any sense.

503
00:46:01,916 --> 00:46:02,916
Did you inform his family?

504
00:46:03,083 --> 00:46:04,165
Yes, sir.

505
00:46:04,166 --> 00:46:06,500
I didn't explain anything.
Just asked them to come.

506
00:46:06,708 --> 00:46:08,499
They're near the border.
They'll reach soon.

507
00:46:08,500 --> 00:46:10,375
Inform me if there's anything else.
- Okay, sir.

508
00:46:10,750 --> 00:46:12,166
- Listen, he regained...

509
00:46:31,083 --> 00:46:33,791
Sir, hello? Hello?

510
00:46:34,000 --> 00:46:35,541
Hello? Hello?

511
00:46:35,958 --> 00:46:37,000
Can you hear me?

512
00:46:37,125 --> 00:46:38,625
Sir, can you hear me?
- Hello? Hello?

513
00:46:39,416 --> 00:46:41,083
Just handle this, man.
- Sir!

514
00:46:41,500 --> 00:46:43,208
Sir, can you hear me?

515
00:46:43,625 --> 00:46:44,375
Hello?

516
00:46:44,500 --> 00:46:45,208
Sir...

517
00:46:45,500 --> 00:46:47,125
We're near the temple.

518
00:46:47,416 --> 00:46:48,916
I'm somewhere close to it, sir.

519
00:46:49,041 --> 00:46:50,375
I'm nearby.

520
00:46:50,500 --> 00:46:52,500
Nearby where?
Ask him for another landmark.

521
00:46:53,125 --> 00:46:55,125
Sir... where exactly are you?

522
00:46:55,541 --> 00:46:58,500
Sir... it's all trees here.

523
00:46:58,916 --> 00:47:00,958
What do you expect
in a forest? Trees or ti...

524
00:47:01,500 --> 00:47:02,833
Go on, go on.

525
00:47:02,958 --> 00:47:04,666
Sir, is it left
or right from here?

526
00:47:05,083 --> 00:47:06,791
Sir, it's left.

527
00:47:08,375 --> 00:47:11,166
No, no! Right, sir.

528
00:47:11,333 --> 00:47:12,583
Are you sure, sir?

529
00:47:12,833 --> 00:47:14,750
Yes, sir. It's right.
- Check that side.

530
00:47:24,916 --> 00:47:26,708
Their ASI is calling.

531
00:47:28,041 --> 00:47:29,041
Hello?

532
00:47:30,291 --> 00:47:31,374
Hello, who is this?

533
00:47:31,375 --> 00:47:33,791
Sir, I'm Ashokan, in
charge at Velloorkadu station.

534
00:47:34,083 --> 00:47:34,708
Yes, tell me, sir.

535
00:47:34,833 --> 00:47:36,750
Sir, we received
information this morning.

536
00:47:36,958 --> 00:47:40,708
That an officer from your
station is trapped in this forest.

537
00:47:41,083 --> 00:47:42,666
We tried contacting you.

538
00:47:42,791 --> 00:47:44,833
Since we couldn't reach you,
we came here ourselves.

539
00:47:44,958 --> 00:47:46,000
Forest?

540
00:47:46,166 --> 00:47:46,916
Which area?

541
00:47:47,041 --> 00:47:49,625
Sir, there's an old temple
deep inside the forest, right?

542
00:47:49,750 --> 00:47:50,790
Seems to be near that.

543
00:47:50,791 --> 00:47:52,666
Oh, temple? Which temple?

544
00:47:52,791 --> 00:47:56,250
An old one...
With a crow statue.

545
00:47:56,375 --> 00:47:57,916
Somewhere near that premises.

546
00:47:59,041 --> 00:48:00,416
That place?

547
00:48:00,875 --> 00:48:02,500
Where exactly are you now?

548
00:48:02,958 --> 00:48:04,625
We're close to it.

549
00:48:04,750 --> 00:48:06,541
Almost near the premises.

550
00:48:07,583 --> 00:48:09,250
Have you lost your minds?

551
00:48:12,583 --> 00:48:14,416
No one from here
would ever go there.

552
00:48:14,541 --> 00:48:16,040
First, leave that
place immediately.

553
00:48:16,041 --> 00:48:18,500
Sir, we spoke to
him just a while ago.

554
00:48:20,166 --> 00:48:21,583
Doesn't he have a name?

555
00:48:22,208 --> 00:48:23,666
I think his name is Stephen.

556
00:48:23,791 --> 00:48:25,416
Sir, you don't even know his name?

557
00:48:25,541 --> 00:48:28,000
Why enter the forest
without basic clarity?

558
00:48:28,166 --> 00:48:29,249
It's Stephen, sir.

559
00:48:29,250 --> 00:48:31,000
Yes, his name is
definitely Stephen.

560
00:48:31,291 --> 00:48:32,791
There's no one by that name here!

561
00:48:33,166 --> 00:48:34,666
First, get out of there!

562
00:48:35,041 --> 00:48:36,041
Please!

563
00:48:54,000 --> 00:48:56,333
Sir, can you hear
me? Can you hear me?

564
00:48:58,000 --> 00:49:00,166
Sir, are you still on the line?

565
00:49:00,375 --> 00:49:02,083
Sir, it's him.

566
00:49:02,875 --> 00:49:04,916
Sir, this feels very
off. Let's leave.

567
00:49:05,041 --> 00:49:07,166
Where are you, sir?

568
00:49:09,625 --> 00:49:11,458
Hey, where are you now?

569
00:49:11,708 --> 00:49:13,541
We've been wandering
around here for so long!

570
00:49:13,666 --> 00:49:14,666
Who are you?

571
00:49:14,833 --> 00:49:17,458
Sir, come on!
My name is Stephen!

572
00:49:19,125 --> 00:49:20,707
Are you really from
Perumalai station?

573
00:49:20,708 --> 00:49:21,458
Yes, sir.

574
00:49:21,583 --> 00:49:24,916
When we called there, they said
no one named Stephen works there.

575
00:49:25,208 --> 00:49:26,583
Who told you that?

576
00:49:26,875 --> 00:49:29,708
Why would I lie to you
in a situation like this?

577
00:49:30,291 --> 00:49:33,458
My name is Stephen George. I'm
the Inspector of Perumalai Station.

578
00:49:33,583 --> 00:49:34,708
Darn! Hold this!

579
00:49:34,833 --> 00:49:37,166
Sir... please believe me.

580
00:49:37,541 --> 00:49:39,416
I'm telling you the truth, sir.

581
00:49:39,916 --> 00:49:41,125
Sir...

582
00:49:41,750 --> 00:49:44,208
I can't beg anymore.

583
00:49:44,333 --> 00:49:46,291
My name is Stephen.

584
00:49:46,791 --> 00:49:49,250
Sir, shall we call
that ASI once more?

585
00:49:49,375 --> 00:49:51,125
Please help me, sir.

586
00:49:52,583 --> 00:49:55,625
If the caste issue escalates, or if
they file a complaint, inform me.

587
00:49:55,750 --> 00:49:57,083
Understood?

588
00:50:01,833 --> 00:50:03,291
What's wrong with you, sir?

589
00:50:03,416 --> 00:50:04,790
Haven't you left that place yet?

590
00:50:04,791 --> 00:50:08,291
Sir, please listen fully
to what I'm saying.

591
00:50:08,541 --> 00:50:11,375
This morning, there was an
accident on the forest route.

592
00:50:11,708 --> 00:50:15,458
The victim was a police officer
named Peter from your station.

593
00:50:15,583 --> 00:50:17,208
We admitted him to the hospital.

594
00:50:17,333 --> 00:50:21,166
After some time,
a message came to his handset.

595
00:50:21,416 --> 00:50:24,083
It said someone was
trapped in this forest.

596
00:50:24,208 --> 00:50:26,250
The information we
received said it was

597
00:50:26,375 --> 00:50:28,625
SI Stephen George
from Perumalai Station.

598
00:50:29,500 --> 00:50:31,041
Apart from this,

599
00:50:31,166 --> 00:50:33,458
we also recovered a body
from the forest this morning.

600
00:50:34,083 --> 00:50:35,875
That too... of a policeman.

601
00:50:36,208 --> 00:50:40,166
Sir, we suspect it might be someone
from Perumalai Police Station.

602
00:50:40,458 --> 00:50:43,125
Sir, please understand
what I'm saying.

603
00:50:43,250 --> 00:50:44,833
There was a meeting
at our station today.

604
00:50:44,958 --> 00:50:46,291
All of us were present.

605
00:50:46,416 --> 00:50:48,083
There are only two
SIs at our station.

606
00:50:48,208 --> 00:50:50,500
One is Ram, and the
other is Principal SI Kumar.

607
00:50:50,625 --> 00:50:53,333
There is no one named Peter
or Stephen at our station!

608
00:51:01,833 --> 00:51:04,458
Then, sir...
who are we talking to?

609
00:51:04,583 --> 00:51:05,916
Why are you asking me all this?

610
00:51:06,041 --> 00:51:07,707
You're just wandering
around for nothing!

611
00:51:07,708 --> 00:51:09,291
And troubling me on top of that!

612
00:51:10,208 --> 00:51:13,250
Sir, he sounds very sure.
He's still on the line.

613
00:51:13,375 --> 00:51:15,041
Please speak to him.

614
00:51:15,458 --> 00:51:17,416
Sir?
- Tell me, sir.

615
00:51:17,541 --> 00:51:19,708
Sir, the ASI from your
station is on the call.

616
00:51:19,833 --> 00:51:21,041
Please speak to him.

617
00:51:21,250 --> 00:51:22,000
ASI?

618
00:51:22,125 --> 00:51:23,291
Isn't it Muthuvel?

619
00:51:23,416 --> 00:51:25,416
Muthuvel, it's me-Stephen.

620
00:51:25,541 --> 00:51:27,125
Where did all of you go!?

621
00:51:27,250 --> 00:51:29,000
I'm all alone here!

622
00:51:29,125 --> 00:51:30,666
Where are the others?

623
00:51:30,791 --> 00:51:32,666
Please come here quickly.

624
00:51:32,791 --> 00:51:35,125
Wait...
what's his full name again?

625
00:51:35,333 --> 00:51:36,791
Stephen George, right?

626
00:51:37,291 --> 00:51:38,791
Yes. Stephen George.

627
00:51:39,291 --> 00:51:41,833
Ask the full name
of that Muthuvel.

628
00:51:43,791 --> 00:51:46,208
Sir, what's
Muthuvel's full name?

629
00:51:46,500 --> 00:51:48,208
Why are you asking
all that, sir?

630
00:51:48,625 --> 00:51:50,041
Just tell us, sir!

631
00:51:50,583 --> 00:51:52,291
Muthuvel Mariyappan.

632
00:51:57,083 --> 00:51:58,541
Hello? Sir?

633
00:51:59,625 --> 00:52:00,791
Sir...

634
00:52:00,916 --> 00:52:03,166
There was an SI named
Stephen in our station.

635
00:52:03,500 --> 00:52:04,708
But not now.

636
00:52:04,833 --> 00:52:06,625
30 years ago!

637
00:52:10,291 --> 00:52:13,000
He and his team went
missing in that forest.

638
00:52:13,666 --> 00:52:15,208
To be exact...

639
00:52:15,416 --> 00:52:17,708
It was on May 26, 1994.

640
00:52:21,666 --> 00:52:24,791
Stephen, Muthuvel,
Peter, Muniswami, Selvam.

641
00:52:25,333 --> 00:52:27,375
And that Muthuvel...
is my father.

642
00:52:31,041 --> 00:52:33,583
After that, no one
has ever seen them.

643
00:52:34,166 --> 00:52:35,791
To be very clear...

644
00:52:36,291 --> 00:52:38,875
There's no way
they're still alive.

645
00:52:41,958 --> 00:52:43,500
Not just them...

646
00:52:43,916 --> 00:52:46,583
No one who went there
ever came back alive.

647
00:52:56,458 --> 00:52:58,250
Didn't I warn you?

648
00:52:58,500 --> 00:53:00,541
That is a very dangerous place.

649
00:53:00,833 --> 00:53:03,291
Get out of there immediately.

650
00:53:04,791 --> 00:53:07,291
Muthuvel! Hey, Muthuvel!
Can you hear me?

651
00:53:08,333 --> 00:53:11,791
Hey! Say something!

652
00:53:13,416 --> 00:53:15,541
Sir, are you coming?
I'm leaving!

653
00:53:15,750 --> 00:53:17,625
Sir, maybe he got
the wrong person.

654
00:53:17,875 --> 00:53:18,957
Otherwise, how can
someone trapped

655
00:53:18,958 --> 00:53:20,541
30 years ago speak
to us now over this?

656
00:53:20,666 --> 00:53:22,166
Hey! Didn't you
hear what he said?

657
00:53:22,291 --> 00:53:23,625
Didn't it sink into your head?

658
00:53:23,750 --> 00:53:27,250
Should we believe what someone
told us, or what we heard ourselves?

659
00:53:27,583 --> 00:53:29,083
I told you from
the start, sir...

660
00:53:29,291 --> 00:53:31,333
We came here because
of this moron!

661
00:53:31,583 --> 00:53:32,916
Sir, don't abuse
me for no reason.

662
00:53:33,041 --> 00:53:35,083
What if I do?
- Try calling me then!

663
00:53:35,208 --> 00:53:37,125
Come on!
- Move aside!

664
00:53:38,375 --> 00:53:40,791
Someone begging for his life
made us enter this forest!

665
00:53:40,916 --> 00:53:43,165
Ashokan won't leave this
place unless this is resolved!

666
00:53:43,166 --> 00:53:46,291
Then you two stay
and solve it yourselves!

667
00:53:49,000 --> 00:53:50,000
Hey, Reji!

668
00:53:50,250 --> 00:53:51,625
Hey!

669
00:53:52,708 --> 00:53:53,875
Sir, sir...

670
00:53:54,333 --> 00:53:55,958
There's a big tree here...

671
00:53:56,416 --> 00:53:58,250
biggest one around.

672
00:53:58,500 --> 00:54:00,458
Covered in thick creepers...

673
00:54:00,583 --> 00:54:02,291
I'm right under it, sir.

674
00:54:02,750 --> 00:54:04,583
Sir, I'm here!

675
00:54:05,541 --> 00:54:06,958
Sir, can you hear me?

676
00:54:07,208 --> 00:54:08,250
Can you hear me!?

677
00:54:39,666 --> 00:54:40,666
Sir...

678
00:54:41,125 --> 00:54:42,833
Did you see the tree?

679
00:54:43,666 --> 00:54:45,916
Please say something, sir.

680
00:54:51,333 --> 00:54:53,250
Sir! Sir!

681
00:54:54,708 --> 00:54:56,333
There's a body here, sir!

682
00:54:56,458 --> 00:54:58,916
I actually tripped
on that and fell down.

683
00:54:59,125 --> 00:55:00,208
Sir...

684
00:55:00,500 --> 00:55:01,541
A body...

685
00:55:01,666 --> 00:55:03,458
It's a policeman's body, sir!

686
00:55:04,166 --> 00:55:05,875
That's not our uniform...

687
00:55:06,333 --> 00:55:07,666
It's Kerala Police.

688
00:55:07,875 --> 00:55:09,750
Kerala Police uniform!

689
00:55:10,916 --> 00:55:13,333
This looks like a
middle-aged man, sir.

690
00:55:14,166 --> 00:55:16,500
This is the body
of an Inspector.

691
00:55:17,041 --> 00:55:19,291
Name tag says Ashokan!

692
00:55:19,791 --> 00:55:21,375
M.G. Ashokan!

693
00:56:14,208 --> 00:56:16,625
Please say something, sir!

694
00:56:22,833 --> 00:56:26,166
Sir, we're running out of time!

695
00:56:28,208 --> 00:56:29,208
Sir...

696
00:56:29,458 --> 00:56:30,875
When did you come here?

697
00:56:31,000 --> 00:56:32,958
It's been around 2-3 hours.

698
00:56:34,125 --> 00:56:35,416
What's today's date?

699
00:56:35,541 --> 00:56:37,541
Why are you asking that now?

700
00:56:37,666 --> 00:56:38,958
Just tell me, sir!

701
00:56:39,083 --> 00:56:40,916
May 26th...

702
00:56:42,625 --> 00:56:44,083
Tell me the year, sir.

703
00:56:44,291 --> 00:56:46,333
1994.

704
00:57:53,750 --> 00:57:56,291
Hey, hurry up!

705
00:57:56,416 --> 00:57:58,083
Careful, Mum.

706
00:57:59,166 --> 00:58:00,166
Be careful.

707
00:58:07,125 --> 00:58:09,208
Sir, where's the ICU?
- That way.

708
00:58:09,333 --> 00:58:11,208
Come on, quick.

709
00:58:13,041 --> 00:58:14,875
No, no.
- We want to see, sir.

710
00:58:15,083 --> 00:58:15,875
Why are you not letting us?

711
00:58:16,000 --> 00:58:17,166
What are you saying, sir?

712
00:58:17,375 --> 00:58:19,958
You can't see him.
Leave with her.

713
00:58:20,125 --> 00:58:21,875
Please let us in, sir.

714
00:58:22,000 --> 00:58:23,458
Sir, we want to see, sir.

715
00:58:23,583 --> 00:58:25,958
No, just move away!

716
00:58:26,541 --> 00:58:27,666
Sir?

717
00:58:28,333 --> 00:58:29,333
Sir?

718
00:58:42,291 --> 00:58:43,875
Hello?
- Sir...

719
00:58:44,166 --> 00:58:45,833
The man who was
admitted to the hospital...

720
00:58:46,208 --> 00:58:47,708
...has passed away.

721
00:58:50,125 --> 00:58:52,125
Sir, there's another issue.

722
00:58:53,208 --> 00:58:54,083
What is it?

723
00:58:54,208 --> 00:58:56,332
Among the people who came
claiming to be his relatives,

724
00:58:56,333 --> 00:58:57,458
there was a woman as well.

725
00:58:57,583 --> 00:58:59,750
She looked to be around 50.

726
00:59:00,166 --> 00:59:01,833
She could be his mother.

727
00:59:02,208 --> 00:59:04,791
That's what the hospital
staff assumed at first.

728
00:59:05,416 --> 00:59:06,708
But...

729
00:59:06,833 --> 00:59:08,250
she isn't his mother.

730
00:59:12,000 --> 00:59:13,125
Then who is she?

731
00:59:13,250 --> 00:59:15,000
I want to see Peter.
Let me go inside.

732
00:59:15,125 --> 00:59:16,166
Let us go in.

733
00:59:16,291 --> 00:59:18,833
You can't create a scene here.
This is a hospital.

734
00:59:18,958 --> 00:59:21,083
Please take your
mother and step outside.

735
00:59:21,208 --> 00:59:23,458
Sir, I can't.
- You can't see him!

736
00:59:23,583 --> 00:59:25,165
This is a hospital.
Don't create a disturbance!

737
00:59:25,166 --> 00:59:26,166
What's going on?

738
00:59:26,375 --> 00:59:29,041
Wait.. What? - I need to see
Peter, but they won't let me in.

739
00:59:29,166 --> 00:59:30,750
What's the problem?
- Sir...

740
00:59:30,958 --> 00:59:32,458
They claim to be
relatives of Peter,

741
00:59:32,583 --> 00:59:34,291
who was admitted
after an accident.

742
00:59:34,416 --> 00:59:37,583
When I asked about their relation,
she said Peter is her husband.

743
00:59:38,958 --> 00:59:39,958
So what?

744
00:59:40,416 --> 00:59:41,416
Sir, didn't you see him?

745
00:59:41,541 --> 00:59:43,625
Peter looks to
be around 30 years.

746
00:59:43,833 --> 00:59:46,124
This looks like a fraud case, sir.
- Hey! Fraud, is it!?

747
00:59:46,125 --> 00:59:47,707
- Who are you calling a fraud?
- Huh?

748
00:59:47,708 --> 00:59:49,499
Who did you just call a fraud?!

749
00:59:49,500 --> 00:59:51,416
We won't allow this here.

750
00:59:51,583 --> 00:59:53,208
Quiet. Let me talk to them.

751
00:59:53,541 --> 00:59:54,790
What happened to your husband?

752
00:59:54,791 --> 00:59:56,666
He went missing in the forest.

753
00:59:56,791 --> 00:59:57,791
When?

754
00:59:57,916 --> 01:00:00,166
Thirty years ago.

755
01:00:00,500 --> 01:00:01,708
Thirty years!?

756
01:00:01,958 --> 01:00:04,208
Mum, the man inside
barely 30 years old.

757
01:00:04,333 --> 01:00:05,416
He can't be your husband.

758
01:00:05,541 --> 01:00:07,083
What? Are you mocking us?

759
01:00:07,208 --> 01:00:09,041
You were the ones
who called us here, right?

760
01:00:09,291 --> 01:00:11,291
Yes, that's true.
But this isn't your person.

761
01:00:11,416 --> 01:00:12,500
Wait a moment, sir.

762
01:00:12,666 --> 01:00:14,541
- You can't see him just like that.
- Sir, sir...

763
01:00:14,875 --> 01:00:16,291
Isn't the man inside the same?

764
01:00:16,416 --> 01:00:18,541
It's the same person.
Just take her and leave.

765
01:00:18,666 --> 01:00:19,749
Confirm it's the same man?

766
01:00:19,750 --> 01:00:20,958
Confirm! Now leave!

767
01:00:21,083 --> 01:00:22,374
This is a hospital.
Don't create trouble here!

768
01:00:22,375 --> 01:00:24,125
Sir, look at his date
of birth on this card.

769
01:00:24,333 --> 01:00:27,875
How can someone born in 1959
still be only 30 years old!?

770
01:00:30,708 --> 01:00:32,541
Sir... he is my father!

771
01:00:57,166 --> 01:00:58,333
Sir...

772
01:00:58,625 --> 01:01:00,416
They're all confused.

773
01:01:03,250 --> 01:01:04,791
What do we do now, sir?

774
01:01:06,083 --> 01:01:07,208
Joshy...

775
01:01:07,708 --> 01:01:09,250
I'll call you back, mate.

776
01:02:45,166 --> 01:02:46,541
Saneesh, tell me.

777
01:02:46,666 --> 01:02:47,708
Sir...

778
01:02:48,083 --> 01:02:50,500
The forensic team had arrived
and started their examination.

779
01:02:52,166 --> 01:02:53,166
Sir...

780
01:02:53,333 --> 01:02:54,541
Is Reji sir with you?

781
01:02:55,333 --> 01:02:56,333
No.

782
01:02:56,708 --> 01:02:59,416
Sir, that body doesn't belong to
anyone from Perumalai station.

783
01:03:01,416 --> 01:03:02,875
That body looks...

784
01:03:03,333 --> 01:03:05,041
exactly like Reji sir.

785
01:03:08,208 --> 01:03:09,833
Saneesh, are you drunk!?

786
01:03:09,958 --> 01:03:10,958
No, sir.

787
01:03:11,541 --> 01:03:12,916
Is Rashid there?

788
01:03:13,041 --> 01:03:14,375
He's not here, sir.

789
01:03:14,958 --> 01:03:16,000
Who else is there?

790
01:03:16,125 --> 01:03:17,208
Akash?

791
01:03:17,333 --> 01:03:19,333
- Yes, sir.
- Put him on the phone.

792
01:03:22,666 --> 01:03:23,791
Sir...

793
01:03:25,666 --> 01:03:27,416
Hey, what's going on?

794
01:03:27,791 --> 01:03:29,541
Sir, even after
cleaning the face...

795
01:03:29,875 --> 01:03:31,625
it still looked like Reji sir.

796
01:03:33,541 --> 01:03:35,291
But we still thought...

797
01:03:35,708 --> 01:03:37,250
it might be someone else.

798
01:03:37,625 --> 01:03:40,208
But when we found
the ID card in his purse...

799
01:03:51,750 --> 01:03:53,708
Sir, haven't you
seen Reji sir's ring?

800
01:03:54,541 --> 01:03:55,916
Everything matches exactly.

801
01:03:56,041 --> 01:03:59,375
Akash, wasn't Reji with us
when we went to see the body!?

802
01:03:59,500 --> 01:04:01,125
Weren't you right
there with me!?

803
01:04:01,583 --> 01:04:02,624
Yes, sir.

804
01:04:02,625 --> 01:04:05,250
Then what the hell
is going on here!?

805
01:04:17,666 --> 01:04:19,000
Sir!

806
01:04:34,875 --> 01:04:35,875
Sir...

807
01:04:38,541 --> 01:04:39,916
Sir!

808
01:04:42,916 --> 01:04:44,416
Ashokan sir!

809
01:04:47,541 --> 01:04:49,041
Sir!

810
01:04:53,416 --> 01:04:55,291
SIR!

811
01:04:59,708 --> 01:05:01,125
Reji...

812
01:05:01,250 --> 01:05:02,416
Reji...

813
01:05:02,541 --> 01:05:03,541
Sir...

814
01:05:08,333 --> 01:05:10,333
Reji sir, grab my hand!

815
01:05:16,708 --> 01:05:18,583
Sir, hold my hand.

816
01:05:19,625 --> 01:05:21,250
Pull him up!

817
01:05:23,958 --> 01:05:24,750
Slowly.

818
01:05:24,958 --> 01:05:26,791
Give your hand.

819
01:05:33,875 --> 01:05:35,500
Reji, come on!

820
01:05:47,416 --> 01:05:48,416
Sir...

821
01:05:49,083 --> 01:05:51,458
Reji sir, give me
your hand! Come on!

822
01:07:13,875 --> 01:07:15,041
Sir!

823
01:07:18,041 --> 01:07:19,416
Sir?

824
01:07:25,833 --> 01:07:26,916
Sir?

825
01:07:38,041 --> 01:07:39,666
James?

826
01:07:42,208 --> 01:07:44,375
James, where are you?

827
01:07:45,708 --> 01:07:48,750
Don't play with me.
Come to me.

828
01:07:53,291 --> 01:07:54,708
James?

829
01:07:54,833 --> 01:07:56,500
Are you there?

830
01:08:07,541 --> 01:08:09,000
Who are you?

831
01:09:05,125 --> 01:09:06,541
What happened?

832
01:09:06,750 --> 01:09:08,791
My brother...

833
01:09:09,000 --> 01:09:10,833
He's missing.

834
01:09:14,041 --> 01:09:15,541
Don't cry. We'll find him.

835
01:09:18,083 --> 01:09:19,375
Wait here, alright?

836
01:10:21,291 --> 01:10:22,750
Dear, go!

837
01:10:25,500 --> 01:10:26,833
Go!

838
01:10:32,875 --> 01:10:34,250
Hey!

839
01:11:37,333 --> 01:11:38,666
Who are you!?

840
01:11:38,791 --> 01:11:40,000
Sir, I'm police.

841
01:11:40,166 --> 01:11:42,125
CPO from Velloorkadu station.

842
01:11:44,500 --> 01:11:45,833
I'm Stephen George.

843
01:11:46,416 --> 01:11:47,958
SI, Perumalai station.

844
01:11:50,083 --> 01:11:51,875
Accused escaped from our bus.

845
01:11:52,250 --> 01:11:53,625
I'm searching for them.

846
01:11:56,375 --> 01:11:57,375
Sir!

847
01:11:57,625 --> 01:11:58,708
What's today's date?

848
01:11:58,916 --> 01:12:00,000
May 26th.

849
01:12:01,208 --> 01:12:02,208
And what year is it?

850
01:12:02,916 --> 01:12:04,250
What? I didn't get you.

851
01:12:04,541 --> 01:12:06,666
I asked, what year is this?

852
01:12:07,375 --> 01:12:08,875
Are you playing games!?

853
01:12:09,333 --> 01:12:10,333
Please, sir.

854
01:12:11,166 --> 01:12:13,291
1994. So what now?

855
01:12:30,500 --> 01:12:32,458
Sir, please save me!

856
01:12:32,833 --> 01:12:34,083
Sir!

857
01:12:34,541 --> 01:12:35,333
Sir!

858
01:12:35,458 --> 01:12:36,625
Sir...

859
01:12:38,083 --> 01:12:39,416
Muthuvel...

860
01:12:39,541 --> 01:12:40,541
Sir...

861
01:12:42,375 --> 01:12:44,125
- Sir, sir.
- What happened, Muthuvel?

862
01:12:44,250 --> 01:12:45,333
These guys!

863
01:12:46,125 --> 01:12:47,875
Hey, calm down and
surrender yourself!

864
01:12:48,000 --> 01:12:49,000
Kill him!

865
01:14:37,000 --> 01:14:38,250
Who are you!?

866
01:14:55,208 --> 01:14:56,791
James...

867
01:15:01,041 --> 01:15:02,458
James?

868
01:15:03,833 --> 01:15:05,750
Where are you hiding?

869
01:15:07,625 --> 01:15:09,416
Don't be scared.

870
01:15:15,750 --> 01:15:16,750
James...

871
01:15:18,750 --> 01:15:19,875
Darling...

872
01:15:31,500 --> 01:15:32,666
James...

873
01:15:33,541 --> 01:15:35,583
Why are you so scared?

874
01:15:36,666 --> 01:15:37,708
Come to me.

875
01:15:38,000 --> 01:15:41,000
Come and kiss me
just like our first time.

876
01:15:41,750 --> 01:15:43,791
Come on! Get up!

877
01:16:41,000 --> 01:16:43,000
Sir, you look
absolutely terrified.

878
01:16:46,208 --> 01:16:47,750
Don't worry, sir.

879
01:16:48,083 --> 01:16:50,208
There are no ghosts
roaming in this forest.

880
01:16:52,541 --> 01:16:53,625
Who are you?

881
01:16:54,833 --> 01:16:56,415
Sir, what exactly do
you want to know?

882
01:16:56,416 --> 01:16:58,041
Who I am or what
is happening here?

883
01:17:02,500 --> 01:17:05,000
Sir, did you notice an
idol on your way here?

884
01:17:05,291 --> 01:17:06,833
Did you observe its head?

885
01:17:07,416 --> 01:17:09,250
It was shaped like a crow.

886
01:17:12,416 --> 01:17:15,541
Since entering this forest,
have you seen even a single crow?

887
01:17:17,583 --> 01:17:18,708
No!

888
01:17:19,291 --> 01:17:22,708
Every problem that happens
here revolves around that.

889
01:17:26,791 --> 01:17:29,250
The origin of all this
goes back many years.

890
01:17:31,083 --> 01:17:32,250
To be precise...

891
01:17:32,708 --> 01:17:35,083
To the time when the
Portuguese first arrived here.

892
01:17:38,166 --> 01:17:39,166
Back then...

893
01:17:39,291 --> 01:17:41,458
this idol was worshipped by

894
01:17:41,791 --> 01:17:44,375
a specific tribe
living in this forest.

895
01:17:46,416 --> 01:17:49,791
They believed crows
as the symbol of God.

896
01:17:52,166 --> 01:17:54,208
They would circle
around this idol,

897
01:17:54,750 --> 01:17:56,541
praying for prosperity
for themselves

898
01:17:56,666 --> 01:17:58,333
and their future generations.

899
01:17:59,500 --> 01:18:03,958
If pregnant women prayed
here and fed the crows,

900
01:18:04,208 --> 01:18:08,375
they believed their unborn child
would be blessed with prosperity.

901
01:18:10,291 --> 01:18:13,125
When Portuguese dominance
reached its peak,

902
01:18:13,416 --> 01:18:17,625
Lord Gabriel Antonio,
a rationalist who ruled this region

903
01:18:17,750 --> 01:18:22,708
decided to erase every belief
that existed here until then.

904
01:18:24,666 --> 01:18:26,666
He followed only one ideology.

905
01:18:27,000 --> 01:18:29,125
'Praises only for the King!'

906
01:18:29,250 --> 01:18:32,000
Worship was meant
for the King alone.

907
01:18:34,041 --> 01:18:36,625
He destroyed every
place of worship here

908
01:18:36,750 --> 01:18:40,000
and smuggled the valuable
idols out of this land.

909
01:18:41,375 --> 01:18:46,625
Eventually, news about
this little-known tribe...

910
01:18:46,750 --> 01:18:49,666
and their unique form of
worship reached the King.

911
01:18:49,791 --> 01:18:53,500
So he entered this forest
with his full army.

912
01:18:53,625 --> 01:18:55,291
To seize that idol!

913
01:18:58,125 --> 01:19:02,500
No matter how much the tribe
pleaded, he refused to listen.

914
01:19:02,916 --> 01:19:07,625
He ordered his forces to take
that idol away at any cost.

915
01:19:11,125 --> 01:19:13,291
But no matter how
hard they tried...

916
01:19:13,416 --> 01:19:15,250
they simply couldn't move it.

917
01:19:16,958 --> 01:19:18,166
Furious at this,

918
01:19:18,291 --> 01:19:20,458
the King ordered the
massacre of the tribe,

919
01:19:20,583 --> 01:19:23,416
hacking them down and
shooting them mercilessly.

920
01:19:24,958 --> 01:19:27,125
Even that wasn't enough for him.

921
01:19:27,333 --> 01:19:30,541
He burned every
crow in this forest.

922
01:19:34,041 --> 01:19:36,958
That bloodshed... was where
everything truly began.

923
01:19:38,333 --> 01:19:40,083
The people believed,

924
01:19:40,541 --> 01:19:44,000
their deity would bring them
prosperity and good fortune.

925
01:19:44,500 --> 01:19:45,666
But...

926
01:19:45,791 --> 01:19:50,250
No one realised it also
had power over time itself.

927
01:19:54,083 --> 01:19:56,625
The King and his forces
took nearly an hour

928
01:19:56,750 --> 01:19:59,208
to reach the temple
through this forest.

929
01:19:59,625 --> 01:20:01,291
But after that massacre...

930
01:20:01,416 --> 01:20:04,583
they couldn't find their way
out, even after a full day.

931
01:20:05,416 --> 01:20:07,416
One day turned
into several days.

932
01:20:07,541 --> 01:20:08,708
Then months,

933
01:20:08,833 --> 01:20:10,333
and eventually years.

934
01:20:11,958 --> 01:20:13,791
Would you believe
me if I said they

935
01:20:13,916 --> 01:20:16,125
are still trapped,
circling this forest?

936
01:20:19,500 --> 01:20:22,125
The moment blood touched
this soil that day,

937
01:20:22,500 --> 01:20:25,083
the deity that had once
been calm and serene

938
01:20:25,708 --> 01:20:27,333
transformed into a
fierce, wrathful force.

939
01:20:29,750 --> 01:20:32,833
From then on, every time
blood was spilled here,

940
01:20:33,416 --> 01:20:35,666
and whenever sound crossed
a certain limit,

941
01:20:36,666 --> 01:20:40,458
even time itself would begin
to distort in this place.

942
01:20:43,083 --> 01:20:46,500
Everyone you saw or heard
here is not dead, sir.

943
01:20:47,208 --> 01:20:49,125
They are people
trapped inside this loop.

944
01:20:50,958 --> 01:20:52,875
From different eras of time.

945
01:21:57,500 --> 01:21:59,125
How do you know all this?

946
01:22:00,958 --> 01:22:04,250
I was the one who betrayed these
people and brought the King here.

947
01:22:04,375 --> 01:22:06,666
A spy for the Portuguese army.

948
01:22:08,625 --> 01:22:11,000
The main reason
behind this entire disaster!

949
01:22:18,625 --> 01:22:19,750
Sir!

950
01:22:19,875 --> 01:22:20,958
Sir!

951
01:22:22,500 --> 01:22:25,500
There is only one
way to escape this, sir.

952
01:22:27,083 --> 01:22:30,083
The incident that brought me,
you, and everyone else here

953
01:22:30,333 --> 01:22:32,000
must never happen!

954
01:22:33,666 --> 01:22:35,166
Until we stop it,

955
01:22:35,708 --> 01:22:38,250
we will remain
trapped in this loop!

956
01:22:52,833 --> 01:22:53,833
Sir!

957
01:22:54,375 --> 01:22:55,458
Ashokan sir!

958
01:23:06,291 --> 01:23:07,750
Sir!

959
01:23:18,666 --> 01:23:20,333
Reji!
- Sir!

960
01:23:24,166 --> 01:23:25,916
Reji!

961
01:23:26,333 --> 01:23:27,750
Sir!

962
01:23:34,666 --> 01:23:37,291
Sir, give me your hand.

963
01:23:41,000 --> 01:23:42,333
Sir!

964
01:23:49,083 --> 01:23:52,041
Reji sir,
come on, hold my hand!

965
01:25:49,000 --> 01:25:50,166
Hey!

966
01:25:52,125 --> 01:25:53,791
Hey, stop!

967
01:25:55,625 --> 01:25:57,458
Where are you going?

968
01:26:00,166 --> 01:26:01,458
Hey!

969
01:26:10,625 --> 01:26:12,250
Sister!

970
01:27:16,750 --> 01:27:17,875
Reji!

971
01:27:19,166 --> 01:27:20,208
Sister!

972
01:27:20,333 --> 01:27:22,166
Hey, wait!

973
01:27:22,291 --> 01:27:23,416
Sister...

974
01:27:27,541 --> 01:27:29,416
Please stop.

975
01:27:30,666 --> 01:27:32,166
Hey!

976
01:27:36,500 --> 01:27:37,750
Muthuvel!
- Sir!

977
01:27:37,875 --> 01:27:40,333
Are you there?

978
01:27:51,375 --> 01:27:52,375
Sir!

979
01:28:01,958 --> 01:28:03,000
Sir!

980
01:28:03,958 --> 01:28:05,166
Reji sir!

981
01:28:08,041 --> 01:28:09,333
Sir, stop!

982
01:28:20,000 --> 01:28:21,041
Hey!

983
01:29:14,000 --> 01:29:14,875
Sir...

984
01:29:15,000 --> 01:29:17,291
Please don't shoot.
I'll explain everything.

985
01:29:32,041 --> 01:29:33,708
Sir, I'm from the Kerala Police.

986
01:29:33,833 --> 01:29:35,458
You need to leave
this place immediately.

987
01:29:35,750 --> 01:29:37,166
Why, sir?

988
01:29:37,291 --> 01:29:38,999
The accused escaped from
our custody during transport.

989
01:29:39,000 --> 01:29:40,125
We are searching for them.

990
01:29:40,250 --> 01:29:41,625
We can deal with that later, sir.

991
01:29:41,750 --> 01:29:43,041
First, you must leave this place.

992
01:29:43,166 --> 01:29:44,207
I can't do that, sir.

993
01:29:44,208 --> 01:29:47,166
Those rascals fired at
two policemen on duty.

994
01:29:47,416 --> 01:29:49,708
Should we spare them
after crossing such limits?

995
01:29:50,125 --> 01:29:51,625
Sir, please try to understand.

996
01:29:51,750 --> 01:29:53,208
This is a dangerous place!

997
01:29:53,333 --> 01:29:54,333
What is it, sir?

998
01:29:54,500 --> 01:29:56,583
Are you also going to repeat
that stupid ghost story?

999
01:29:58,583 --> 01:29:59,583
Sir!

1000
01:29:59,708 --> 01:30:03,625
If you don't leave now, you will
never see your wife and child again.

1001
01:30:05,541 --> 01:30:07,333
You are going to have a baby.

1002
01:30:07,625 --> 01:30:08,625
A baby boy.

1003
01:30:09,041 --> 01:30:10,166
Who are you?

1004
01:30:13,208 --> 01:30:14,583
How do you know all this?

1005
01:30:14,875 --> 01:30:17,541
My name is Anand. My
mother's name is Sethulakshmi.

1006
01:30:17,875 --> 01:30:19,041
I don't have a father.

1007
01:30:19,166 --> 01:30:20,791
I haven't seen him until now.

1008
01:30:21,125 --> 01:30:22,958
I don't even know
what happened to him.

1009
01:30:23,083 --> 01:30:24,124
But...

1010
01:30:24,125 --> 01:30:25,916
I'm starting to understand it,
piece by piece.

1011
01:30:26,208 --> 01:30:29,166
He went missing in
this forest 30 years ago.

1012
01:30:29,291 --> 01:30:30,750
And he never returned.

1013
01:30:30,875 --> 01:30:33,583
I have only seen my
father in photographs.

1014
01:30:33,791 --> 01:30:35,500
This is my father.

1015
01:30:35,625 --> 01:30:37,166
Stephen George!

1016
01:30:50,833 --> 01:30:51,833
Oh...

1017
01:30:52,041 --> 01:30:53,666
Do you need more proof?

1018
01:30:57,458 --> 01:30:59,875
May 26th, 1994.

1019
01:31:00,000 --> 01:31:01,666
My date of birth.

1020
01:31:01,791 --> 01:31:04,000
The day your son was born.

1021
01:31:13,958 --> 01:31:16,125
Now, the bats will start
screeching together.

1022
01:31:24,000 --> 01:31:26,583
And you will hear a
sound from that side.

1023
01:31:28,333 --> 01:31:32,333
They are going to choke one of
the cops from your team to death.

1024
01:31:33,625 --> 01:31:35,625
If you go there right now,

1025
01:31:35,750 --> 01:31:37,125
you can save him.

1026
01:31:37,250 --> 01:31:38,290
But...

1027
01:31:38,291 --> 01:31:40,416
The moment you fire your gun,

1028
01:31:40,750 --> 01:31:43,208
everything will begin
again from square one.

1029
01:31:43,666 --> 01:31:45,791
Sir, save me!

1030
01:31:46,416 --> 01:31:47,666
Sir!

1031
01:32:15,208 --> 01:32:16,916
Muthuvel!
- Sir!

1032
01:32:18,000 --> 01:32:19,500
What happened, Muthuvel?

1033
01:32:19,625 --> 01:32:21,000
Sir, sir!

1034
01:32:21,125 --> 01:32:22,125
It's them!

1035
01:32:30,125 --> 01:32:31,125
Hey!

1036
01:32:31,250 --> 01:32:32,875
We can't just let them go, sir.

1037
01:32:33,000 --> 01:32:34,458
Why don't you understand?

1038
01:32:34,583 --> 01:32:36,208
Let's catch them once
we get out of here.

1039
01:32:36,333 --> 01:32:38,375
Right now, all of us need
to leave this place first.

1040
01:32:42,208 --> 01:32:44,000
Please...
we need to get out of here.

1041
01:32:44,125 --> 01:32:45,958
Call the others
who are with you.

1042
01:32:46,416 --> 01:32:47,832
Please don't shoot
under any circumstance.

1043
01:32:47,833 --> 01:32:49,958
No blood should
touch this ground.

1044
01:32:58,291 --> 01:32:59,291
Peter...

1045
01:32:59,750 --> 01:33:03,500
If you move a little ahead from
where we split, there's a temple.

1046
01:33:03,625 --> 01:33:05,166
Come there quickly. Over.

1047
01:33:05,291 --> 01:33:07,041
Okay, sir. Over.

1048
01:33:07,291 --> 01:33:10,041
Don't tell sir about Selva for now.

1049
01:33:11,791 --> 01:33:13,958
If he finds out, he won't
leave without catching them.

1050
01:33:14,083 --> 01:33:15,125
But what if he asks?

1051
01:33:15,250 --> 01:33:16,958
We'll make something up if so.

1052
01:33:40,333 --> 01:33:41,333
Sir...

1053
01:33:41,583 --> 01:33:42,875
Which way should
we go from here?

1054
01:33:43,291 --> 01:33:45,125
No matter which way
we go from here, we

1055
01:33:45,333 --> 01:33:46,875
should be able to
reach the road, sir.

1056
01:33:47,708 --> 01:33:48,916
Move ahead.

1057
01:34:36,250 --> 01:34:37,541
Sir!

1058
01:34:52,208 --> 01:34:54,958
Sir, let's try going
through this route.

1059
01:34:58,708 --> 01:34:59,916
Come on, sir.

1060
01:35:00,875 --> 01:35:01,916
Anand...

1061
01:35:31,833 --> 01:35:32,958
Careful.

1062
01:36:59,750 --> 01:37:02,333
Sir, maybe we should
split up and move.

1063
01:37:02,458 --> 01:37:04,583
You take that route.
We'll go this way.

1064
01:37:05,916 --> 01:37:06,916
Anand...

1065
01:37:07,875 --> 01:37:08,875
Be careful.

1066
01:37:09,458 --> 01:37:10,458
Come.

1067
01:38:19,625 --> 01:38:21,207
Didn't I already
warn you we'd be in

1068
01:38:21,208 --> 01:38:22,666
serious trouble if
we came here, sir?

1069
01:38:23,875 --> 01:38:26,416
So, is there really no
way out of this place, sir?

1070
01:38:50,000 --> 01:38:52,666
I know someone who actually
made it out of here alive.

1071
01:40:23,958 --> 01:40:26,750
Didn't you say we could get out no
matter which direction we walked?

1072
01:40:27,708 --> 01:40:30,250
Now let's try circling
around this one.

1073
01:40:34,000 --> 01:40:35,000
Come on, let's move.

1074
01:41:40,541 --> 01:41:41,541
Hello?

1075
01:41:48,625 --> 01:41:49,625
Sir...

1076
01:41:50,291 --> 01:41:52,541
I think we've reached
somewhere close to the road.

1077
01:42:31,208 --> 01:42:32,291
Where's Muthuvel?

1078
01:42:32,541 --> 01:42:34,000
Muthuvel!

1079
01:42:36,000 --> 01:42:37,583
Hey, Muthuvel!

1080
01:42:43,333 --> 01:42:44,458
Muthuvel...

1081
01:42:44,583 --> 01:42:45,583
Muthuvel!

1082
01:42:46,500 --> 01:42:47,791
Hey, Muthuvel!

1083
01:43:01,041 --> 01:43:02,041
Sir...

1084
01:43:02,583 --> 01:43:03,707
We shouldn't stay
here any longer.

1085
01:43:03,708 --> 01:43:04,708
Come.

1086
01:43:06,166 --> 01:43:07,291
Let's go.

1087
01:43:35,166 --> 01:43:36,166
Hey!

1088
01:43:37,083 --> 01:43:38,291
Come.

1089
01:43:42,375 --> 01:43:44,500
From now on, we
move only as a group!

1090
01:44:00,208 --> 01:44:01,208
Hey!

1091
01:45:22,416 --> 01:45:25,041
Peter, are you alright?

1092
01:45:58,541 --> 01:45:59,625
Come on, you!

1093
01:47:20,458 --> 01:47:21,916
Sir, let's move.

1094
01:47:24,791 --> 01:47:26,916
Anand, come on, let's go.

1095
01:47:44,875 --> 01:47:45,875
Hey, Peter!

1096
01:47:46,583 --> 01:47:47,583
Peter...

1097
01:47:48,750 --> 01:47:49,958
Peter!

1098
01:47:50,500 --> 01:47:52,083
What happened, Peter?

1099
01:47:54,750 --> 01:47:55,958
Hey, Peter!

1100
01:47:56,750 --> 01:47:58,416
I can't move forward, sir.

1101
01:48:09,750 --> 01:48:10,916
Peter...

1102
01:48:11,416 --> 01:48:13,083
I'm fine now, sir.

1103
01:48:15,750 --> 01:48:17,208
Get up.

1104
01:49:26,416 --> 01:49:28,250
James!

1105
01:49:28,500 --> 01:49:30,416
Where are you?

1106
01:50:45,750 --> 01:50:46,333
Sir...

1107
01:50:46,458 --> 01:50:47,707
It's coming from that side, sir.

1108
01:50:47,708 --> 01:50:48,708
Come.

1109
01:50:50,500 --> 01:50:51,125
Sir...

1110
01:50:51,250 --> 01:50:52,708
Isn't it coming
from that direction?

1111
01:51:04,708 --> 01:51:06,458
Sir, I'm certain
it's from there.

1112
01:51:11,375 --> 01:51:12,541
Yes, it's from there.

1113
01:51:13,083 --> 01:51:15,166
Hey, he's trying
to confuse us, sir!

1114
01:51:25,250 --> 01:51:26,666
It's from this side, Anand.

1115
01:51:27,458 --> 01:51:29,291
Sir, we just heard
the sound from there.

1116
01:51:29,625 --> 01:51:31,375
Who are you? Why
are you misleading us?

1117
01:51:31,500 --> 01:51:32,083
Hey, Peter!

1118
01:51:32,208 --> 01:51:33,041
Just listen to me.

1119
01:51:33,166 --> 01:51:34,333
Who the heck is he, sir?

1120
01:51:34,625 --> 01:51:36,125
Why are you even trusting him?

1121
01:51:36,416 --> 01:51:38,250
We've come this far
because of what you said.

1122
01:51:38,416 --> 01:51:39,875
Everyone who was with us is dead.

1123
01:51:40,000 --> 01:51:41,375
Now it's just us left.

1124
01:51:41,500 --> 01:51:43,208
Do you want us dead too?

1125
01:51:44,958 --> 01:51:47,000
That crow's call came
from that side, right?

1126
01:51:47,833 --> 01:51:48,833
Come on!

1127
01:52:42,708 --> 01:52:45,875
What? Couldn't you
find any better way to die?

1128
01:52:46,125 --> 01:52:47,625
We are police officers, man!

1129
01:52:49,708 --> 01:52:50,750
What's today's date?

1130
01:52:50,875 --> 01:52:53,166
Sir... May... 26th.

1131
01:52:53,291 --> 01:52:55,250
- Year?
- '94, sir.

1132
01:52:57,541 --> 01:52:59,708
Sir, is there some problem?

1133
01:53:00,833 --> 01:53:01,833
Get in.

1134
01:53:07,500 --> 01:53:08,625
Careful.

1135
01:53:08,750 --> 01:53:10,041
Anand, aren't you coming?

1136
01:53:10,208 --> 01:53:12,291
I can't survive here like this.

1137
01:53:17,291 --> 01:53:18,708
Go and see your baby.

1138
01:53:19,166 --> 01:53:20,541
Stay with him.

1139
01:53:22,541 --> 01:53:25,000
Growing up without
a father is very hard.

1140
01:54:45,625 --> 01:54:46,708
Anand...

1141
01:54:48,666 --> 01:54:50,333
what happened?

1142
01:54:54,208 --> 01:54:55,916
Nothing.

1143
01:54:57,666 --> 01:55:00,000
Neetu's bystander?

1144
01:55:03,583 --> 01:55:04,583
Dad...

1145
01:55:16,666 --> 01:55:18,541
Its a girl.
- Okay!

1146
01:55:18,750 --> 01:55:20,666
Neetu?
- She's fine.

1147
01:55:44,750 --> 01:55:47,000
Sir, which station were
you posted at before this?

1148
01:55:47,125 --> 01:55:48,208
Udayamperoor.

1149
01:55:48,333 --> 01:55:49,333
Oh...

1150
01:55:49,458 --> 01:55:51,125
Benny sir is still there, right?

1151
01:55:51,250 --> 01:55:52,332
Yeah. How do you know him?

1152
01:55:52,333 --> 01:55:54,666
I was posted there in 2019.

1153
01:55:54,791 --> 01:55:56,958
It's been a long time
since I spoke to him.

1154
01:55:57,083 --> 01:55:58,249
How long have you been here?

1155
01:55:58,250 --> 01:55:59,708
Almost a year.

1156
01:55:59,833 --> 01:56:01,666
It's very peaceful here, sir.

1157
01:56:02,375 --> 01:56:04,375
Is Perumalai station nearby?

1158
01:56:04,500 --> 01:56:05,500
Yes, sir.

1159
01:56:05,958 --> 01:56:08,916
Sir, after this
border, it's their area.

1160
01:56:09,041 --> 01:56:10,125
Why did you ask, sir?

1161
01:56:10,250 --> 01:56:12,250
My dad was an inspector there.

1162
01:56:12,541 --> 01:56:14,291
Is your dad a Tamilian?

1163
01:56:14,416 --> 01:56:16,458
So you must know
Tamil very well, right?

1164
01:56:16,583 --> 01:56:17,583
No...

1165
01:56:17,916 --> 01:56:19,208
My mom is a Malayali.

1166
01:56:19,333 --> 01:56:21,375
I've been in Kerala
since childhood.

1167
01:56:23,291 --> 01:56:25,250
Sir, isn't that
Ashokan sir's car?

1168
01:56:25,791 --> 01:56:27,208
Yes, it is.

1169
01:56:31,791 --> 01:56:33,458
What happened, sir?

1170
01:56:35,875 --> 01:56:37,208
My car broke down, man.

1171
01:56:38,291 --> 01:56:39,833
Sir... our new ASI.

1172
01:56:40,625 --> 01:56:43,041
Sir, I'm Ashokan.

1173
01:56:43,541 --> 01:56:45,500
I received a mail saying
you'd be joining today.

1174
01:56:45,708 --> 01:56:48,166
I started earlier to reach there,
but my car ran into trouble.

1175
01:56:48,666 --> 01:56:50,625
Rajesh from the workshop
will be here soon...

1176
01:56:50,750 --> 01:56:53,416
Once he arrives, get this fixed
and take the car to the station.

1177
01:56:54,750 --> 01:56:56,208
Sir, I'll also
come to the station.

1178
01:56:57,666 --> 01:56:59,125
Call me if there's anything.

1179
01:56:59,250 --> 01:57:00,333
Let's go.

1180
01:57:05,125 --> 01:57:06,250
Sir, where is your hometown?

1181
01:57:06,625 --> 01:57:07,708
Kochi.

1182
01:57:08,125 --> 01:57:08,833
Oh!

1183
01:57:08,958 --> 01:57:10,791
So you're a Kochi folk?

1184
01:57:12,541 --> 01:57:14,333
Sir, your family?

1185
01:57:14,875 --> 01:57:16,875
Mom, dad, wife, and daughter.

1186
01:57:17,416 --> 01:57:19,041
How old is your daughter?

1187
01:57:20,250 --> 01:57:21,750
She was born recently.

1188
01:57:21,875 --> 01:57:24,000
Wow, then you owe
us a treat, sir!

1189
01:57:26,666 --> 01:57:27,916
Yes, Rasheed, tell me.

1190
01:57:28,041 --> 01:57:29,166
Sir, there's an issue.

1191
01:57:29,666 --> 01:57:30,666
What issue?

1192
01:57:30,791 --> 01:57:32,791
While passing through
the forest road...

1193
01:57:33,250 --> 01:57:36,083
We noticed a vehicle parked
suspiciously and checked it.

1194
01:57:36,208 --> 01:57:38,250
Some youngsters were inside.

1195
01:57:38,375 --> 01:57:41,291
They were trying to shoot a
video. They're Tamilians, sir.

1196
01:57:41,791 --> 01:57:43,916
There are 1-2 girls
with them as well.

1197
01:57:44,041 --> 01:57:45,625
Sir, he has stepped
in and blocked them!

1198
01:57:45,750 --> 01:57:46,832
Who? Reji?

1199
01:57:46,833 --> 01:57:47,541
Yes, sir.

1200
01:57:47,666 --> 01:57:48,708
Looks like those guys have

1201
01:57:48,833 --> 01:57:50,375
some influence
over higher officials.

1202
01:57:50,500 --> 01:57:51,915
I don't think I can
handle this alone.

1203
01:57:51,916 --> 01:57:53,375
Sir, can you come here quickly?

1204
01:57:54,750 --> 01:57:57,083
What's wrong with him?

1205
01:58:23,708 --> 01:58:26,333
What happened, sir?
- No, nothing.

1206
01:58:29,208 --> 01:58:31,125
Shouldn't you be more careful, man?

1207
01:58:47,041 --> 01:58:50,291
'If you want to call anyone, call
from my phone. - Congrats, uncle.'

1208
01:59:06,416 --> 01:59:07,583
Are you okay?

1209
01:59:07,791 --> 01:59:10,250
Are you okay?

1210
01:59:11,541 --> 01:59:13,833
Hello? Hello?

1211
01:59:14,000 --> 01:59:16,708
Are you okay?

1212
01:59:23,875 --> 01:59:25,458
Come, help me!

1213
01:59:27,041 --> 01:59:28,875
Sir, open the door!

1214
01:59:30,958 --> 01:59:32,541
Move inside, move inside!

1215
01:59:32,666 --> 01:59:34,333
Sir, move inside!

1216
01:59:36,916 --> 01:59:38,500
Go, start the vehicle quickly!

1217
01:59:51,666 --> 01:59:53,082
Hey, breathe.
- Have you seen this girl before?

1218
01:59:53,083 --> 01:59:53,416
No, sir.

1219
01:59:53,541 --> 01:59:55,125
Sir, go faster!

1220
01:59:55,250 --> 01:59:57,333
Hey, open your eyes!

1221
01:59:57,708 --> 01:59:59,166
Floor it, man!

1222
01:59:59,291 --> 02:00:02,750
Sir, take her phone. Check her
recent calls and contact someone.

1223
02:00:03,833 --> 02:00:05,333
Go, go!

1224
02:00:22,541 --> 02:00:23,625
Hey!

1225
02:00:27,375 --> 02:00:28,375
Hey!

1226
02:00:29,500 --> 02:00:32,250
Dad...

1227
02:00:33,541 --> 02:00:35,250
Hey...

1228
02:00:36,333 --> 02:00:37,541
Huh?

1229
02:00:39,333 --> 02:00:40,541
Hey!

1230
02:00:42,541 --> 02:00:43,541
Hey!

1231
02:00:48,791 --> 02:00:49,791
Hey!

1232
02:00:58,000 --> 02:01:00,250
Sir, stop the vehicle.

1233
02:01:48,250 --> 02:01:49,291
Hello?

1234
02:01:49,500 --> 02:01:50,582
Neetu...

1235
02:01:50,583 --> 02:01:51,875
Where is our daughter?

1236
02:01:52,750 --> 02:01:55,208
I'm trying to make her sleep,
but she's very cranky.

1237
02:01:55,333 --> 02:01:56,791
Did you reach there?

1238
02:01:58,958 --> 02:02:00,125
Hello?

1239
02:02:00,875 --> 02:02:02,333
Can't you hear me?

1240
02:02:02,833 --> 02:02:03,916
Hello?

1241
02:02:04,041 --> 02:02:05,333
What happened?

1242
02:02:06,791 --> 02:02:07,541
Nothing.

1243
02:02:07,666 --> 02:02:09,583
Hey, are you okay?

1244
02:02:34,833 --> 02:02:37,541
There is only one
way to escape this, sir.

1245
02:02:38,416 --> 02:02:41,291
The incident that brought me,
you, and everyone else here,

1246
02:02:41,416 --> 02:02:42,750
must not happen!

1247
02:02:48,083 --> 02:02:49,708
Until we stop it,

1248
02:02:50,000 --> 02:02:52,500
we will remain
trapped in this loop!



